From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:42:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: convert the dumpstate HAL from HIDL 1.1 to AIDL

lineage-24.0 deleted hardware/interfaces/dumpstate/1.0 and 1.1; only the
AIDL interface remains. Soong analyses every Android.bp regardless of
PRODUCT_PACKAGES, so the HIDL service failed the whole build:
  dumpstate/Android.bp: "android.hardware.dumpstate@1.1-service.bonito"
  depends on undefined module "android.hardware.dumpstate@1.0"

Same board dumps, same rc actions, same sepolicy domain
(hal_dumpstate_impl). Registered as IDumpstateDevice/default via
libbinder_ndk; the HIDL block is dropped from manifest.xml in favour of a
vintf fragment.
---
 device.mk                                     |   2 +-
 dumpstate/Android.bp                          |  10 +-
 dumpstate/DumpstateDevice.cpp                 | 106 +++++++++---------
 dumpstate/DumpstateDevice.h                   |  47 +++-----
 ...droid.hardware.dumpstate-service.bonito.rc |   8 ++
 ...roid.hardware.dumpstate-service.bonito.xml |   7 ++
 ...d.hardware.dumpstate@1.1-service.bonito.rc |   9 --
 dumpstate/service.cpp                         |  29 ++---
 manifest.xml                                  |   9 --
 sepolicy/vendor/qcom/common/file_contexts     |   1 +
 10 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 130 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dumpstate/android.hardware.dumpstate-service.bonito.rc
 create mode 100644 dumpstate/android.hardware.dumpstate-service.bonito.xml
 delete mode 100644 dumpstate/android.hardware.dumpstate@1.1-service.bonito.rc

